marta: Heads-up — I'm opening a tiny PR to consolidate the SDK snippets for 429/timeouts into a single canonical example. Also doing link fixes for the errref.
sam: thanks — can you include an explicit retry-header example? the repo still has two slightly different variants.
marta: yep, plan is to replace both with one vetted snippet and a short migration note about context trimming.
lia: product asked for a one-liner about graceful fallback to a smaller model when 429s hit at scale.
marta: can you paste the exact suggested wording? prefer we keep it concise.
lia: suggestion: "If you experience sustained 429s, enable quick-fallback routing to a compatible lower-capacity model to preserve throughput while you troubleshoot." short and actionable.
kevin: also a practical nit — the JS example in the docs uses "x-retry-after" header. we standardized around "retry-after" in the SDKs. probably worth showing backoff+jitter too.
