marta: adding a small JS snippet with exponential backoff + jitter to the SDK examples section:
```js
// minimal retry w/ jitter example for 429s
async function callWithRetry(sdk, req) {
  let backoff = 100; // ms
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    try {
      return await sdk.text.generate(req);
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.status === 429) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff + Math.random() * backoff));
        backoff *= 2;
        continue;
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('retries exhausted');
}
```
sam: small nit: use SDK v2 naming in the sample (e.g., `new Redwood({}).responses.create(...)` or the canonical method we publish) — avoid legacy calls.
marta: good catch, i'll update to canonical call pattern and include the `retry-after` header example.
